# the screen reader (fm1-reader, announce.c): a reader listens, and each page, knob and button message is
# said once, in the screen's own text (the words file says it in full); the header when it starts, and on WHERE
wait 200
listen
wait 100
said Tine page: Material Steel, Hardness 45, Decay 50, Tone 55. C Major
# a page, once it settles
tap ENV
wait 300
said Body page: Body Box, Buzz 0, Wah 0, Wah rate Off
# a knob: its name and value, once it settles
spin K2 3
wait 300
said Buzz 3
# a body without a sound hole: the wah greyed, said as such; turning it is a warning
spin K1 -1
wait 300
said Body Board
spin K3 1
wait 50
said NO HOLE BOX OR GOURD
tap SEL
tap ENV
wait 300
said Wah off, no sound hole
# the encoders
turn SELECT 1
wait 300
said Material Brass
turn ALGO 1
wait 300
said Scale Minor
turn PRESET 1
wait 300
said Key C#
# the Keys page follows the layout: Keyboard is said as a new page
tap SEL
wait 300
said Keys page: Layout Tine, Scale Minor, Key C#, Black Chords
spin K1 1
wait 300
said Keys page: Layout Keyboard, Transpose 0, Octave 0
# the buttons' messages (OCT+ says its own: not again as a readout)
tap PLAY
said GRAINS FROZEN
tap ARP
said PATTERN Thumbs
tap REC
said PALM MUTE
tap OCT+
wait 300
said Octave +1
tap SAVE
said SAVED
# MIDI moving a knob
midi B0 48 7F
wait 300
said Decay 100
# WHERE: everything again, the header's chips too
where
said Keys page: Layout Keyboard, Transpose 0, Octave +1. Keyboard. Grains frozen. Pattern on
